4. Boot time optimization (target: 12s → <4s to serial login prompt):

   Already done in repo:
   ✅ MB1/MB2 logging disabled (TEGRA_MB1_LOG_LEVEL = "0")
   ✅ BPMP combined UART disabled (TEGRA_BPMP_SERIAL_LOGGING = "0", deletes /serial from BPMP DTB)
   ✅ EEPROM read disabled (cvb_eeprom_read_size = 0x0)
   ✅ quiet loglevel=0 audit=0 in kernel args
   ✅ No initramfs
   ✅ extlinux timeout = 0
   ✅ UEFI stripped (USB/display/network boot/memory test/serial console)
   ✅ bootlogd + dmesg.sh removed from rcS
   ✅ A/B verifier (userspace) made non-blocking
   ✅ Ethernet deferred to after login prompt

   Remaining (in priority order):
   ❌ #1 Make Docker + containerd init scripts non-blocking (background &) — est. 2-4s saving
   ❌ #2 Make nvidia-container-setup (S50) non-blocking — runs before login, can defer
   ❌ #3 Profile pre-kernel time: run `cat /proc/tegra_boot_times` on board to see MB1/MB2/UEFI split
   ❌ #4 Audit nvstartup (priority 00 in rcS) — runs first, check if it blocks
   ❌ #5 Disable A/B slot check in MB2 bootloader (we always reflash, ~50-100ms saving)

   Note: Docker start can be deferred — app inside container tolerates waiting for its own
   dependencies, so login prompt does not need to wait for Docker to be ready.
  ✅ DONE - validate-boot.py checks Docker (engine+compose), NTP (chronyd), NVIDIA runtime

